## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext module
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.module@1.0
  desc: |
    An ESM namespace module following the DXOS namespace-module styleguide:
    a PascalCase file in src/, re-exported from index.ts as
    `export * as <Name> from './<Name>'`. Callers import it as a namespace, so
    members are unprefixed (`Obj.make`, not `makeObj`). The file path is inferred
    from the block name (`Obj` -> `src/Obj.ts`).
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    api: ApiMap         # public members reached as `<Name>.<member>`  (name: TypeExpr # comment)
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true ("Bounds are derived, never stored."), not as the edit
    that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```
